# C044: Exception-class globals are dangling borrowed pointers after attribute replacement
#
# CONFIRMED — static analysis (use-after-free / reference ownership)
#
# Most exception classes are added with PyModule_AddObject (steals ref), leaving
# process-global C pointers (exc_descriptors[i].cls, ExcConnectionClosed, etc.)
# that do not own a reference.  Users can replace/delete module attributes,
# dropping the last strong reference.  C code then passes the stale pointer to
# exception APIs.  APSWException uses PyModule_AddObjectRef (owned) and is not
# affected the same way.
#
# Runtime testing showed refcount=5 for TooBigError (from module dict, type
# hierarchy, etc.) so replacing the attribute alone didn't free it, but the C
# pointer remains unowned/borrowed.
